  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The product of a certain integer and twice that integer is 32. What can the integer be?\n\nIntroduce a pronumeral, write down a quadratic equation and solve it.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4$ or $-4$",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the integer.\n$$\\begin{align*}n(2n)&=32\\\\2n^2&=32\\\\n^2-16&=0\\\\(n-4)(n+4)&=0\\\\n-4&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n+4=0\\\\n&=4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n=-4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots are integers. The integer can be $4$ or $-4$.\n\nCheck: $4\\times8=32$ and $(-4)\\times(-8)=32$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
